module std::fs;

// File primitives (Rust's std::fs shape: functions returning values; errors
// are simulation/compile failures).
// Runtime-provided, like std::rand. std ships the PRIMITIVE only: format
// loaders (hex images, CSV stimulus, ...) are parsing libraries, not std.
//
//   read<string>(path)     decodes UTF-8 into Char values. The compiler bakes
//                          a hardware/top initializer; a #[test] owns runtime
//                          Char[] length and code-point storage.
//   read<integer>(path)    reads raw little-endian binary integers.
//   read<T>(path)          reads those integers and constructs T from each one,
//                          e.g. `let rom: unsigned[16][256] =
//                          read<unsigned[16]>("rom.bin");`. Each value consumes
//                          ceil(T'length / 8) bytes. Short data zero-fills; data
//                          beyond the scalar/array target is an error. Hardware
//                          reads occur during compilation; #[test] reads occur
//                          in the generated executable.
//   exists(path)           runtime path probe in a #[test] (never fails)
